From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 17:54:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 119/144] GreatDANE: one Dane wordmark for the stock
 firefox-wordmark.svg chrome URL (round 4e)

Stock new-tab and private-browsing CSS already load chrome://branding/content/firefox-wordmark.svg
(and About loads about-wordmark.svg). Those CSS files are not edited. The two greatdane SVGs were
already identical plain-text "Dane" marks; this makes about-wordmark.svg the single source of truth
and aliases firefox-wordmark.svg to it in content/jar.mn, so the stock filename can stay.

about-wordmark.svg is still a plain text "Dane" on a transparent ground. fill is now
"context-fill #13254A": stock CSS can set the color via -moz-context-properties, and the
fallback is the navy from about-logo.svg. The leftover duplicate firefox-wordmark.svg file is
removed.

chrome://browser/skin/window-firefox.svg (Preferences homepage icon) is overridden to
greatdane-icon.svg, the same chrome-registry pattern as the existing sidebar/firefox.svg
override. The stock icon file is unchanged, so official branding is unaffected.

New-tab builtin-addon assets (Discovery Stream firefox.svg, mascot/motion/wallpaper art),
the toolkit ML mozilla-logo.webp, and other shared-tree leftovers are documented in
greatdane/WORDMARK-SOURCES.md and are not swapped, because a file edit would leak into
official branding and a browser.jar override is not assumed to apply to chrome://newtab/.

No Firefox feature is disabled. Official branding paths are untouched. Not a trademark
clearance.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
